{{!-- Collapsible tab search: a round magnifying-glass button that expands into a
      filter box when clicked. Sits to the right of a tab's header text and filters
      that whole tab client-side (see wireTabSearch in StonetopCharacterSheet).
      Caller passes `title` (button tooltip / aria label) and `placeholder`.

      `stonetop-section-heading-control` marks it as a control that RIDES IN a heading rather
      than in the content below it, so folding the section takes it along — see
      _wireSectionCollapse. Without it, a search box would be left hovering over nothing.

      `searchPinned` is the OTHER shape: a box that is already open and never shuts, for a tab
      whose search is the first thing on the page rather than a control tucked in beside a
      heading (the Preferences tab). There is no toggle button in that shape — a button whose
      only job is to shut a box that cannot shut is a dead control — so the glyph is a plain
      `<i>` and the input carries the accessible name on its own. `wireTabSearch` wires a
      control with no toggle, and leaves a pinned box open when it loses focus.

      NAMED `searchPinned` AND NOT `pinned`: this partial is reached from ~45 section headings,
      many of them inside `{{#each}}` loops, and Handlebars merges a partial's hash into the
      caller's context — so a bare `pinned` here would also match a view-model field of that
      name and quietly turn some other tab's search into a shape it never asked for. The long
      name is the same precaution section-heading.hbs spells out at length for its own
      parameters. --}}
<span class="stonetop-tab-search stonetop-section-heading-control{{#if searchPinned}} stonetop-tab-search--pinned{{/if}}" role="search">
	{{#if searchPinned}}
	<i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass stonetop-tab-search-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></i>
	{{else}}
	<button type="button" class="stonetop-tab-search-toggle" title="{{title}}" aria-label="{{title}}">
		<i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass" aria-hidden="true"></i>
	</button>
	{{/if}}
	<input type="search" class="stonetop-tab-search-input" placeholder="{{placeholder}}" aria-label="{{title}}">
</span>
